  Hmm, but hold on — should I double-check the A1 premise once more? Grok's evidence: "当晚 actions=0 是旁证" and audit:173 default. If the runner in the container at the time of those nights was old (pre-r181 deployed 09-05), all consistent. The r2 extrapolation is "r175 旧 runner 未调用" — describing the CURRENT production runner as r175's. But R0/§1 also say current image is r181-20260905. So r2 simultaneously claims: image=r181 (contains guard, per its own guard check) AND runner=r175 (no login_sign). Given f691abb ⋖ f071c85, these two claims are mutually inconsistent unless the image build deliberately mixed versions — no evidence of that.

